// Self-centered burst hitting nearby chosen foes -- the sheet's 2 m range
// is short enough to treat as the burst's own radius rather than a
// separate travel distance, so this uses Explosion the same way
// thunderclap.ron does (see that file for why Explosion is always
// caster-centered and always hardcodes DamageKind::Crushing regardless of
// RON content -- true in-engine damage here is Crushing, not Radiant,
// flavor-only mismatch).
//
// Same AoE-cantrip discount as thunderclap.ron: below the single-target
// cantrip baseline (14) since it can hit multiple nearby foes at once,
// matching real D&D's own Word of Radiance die (1d6, below Fire Bolt's
// 1d10).
Explosion(
    energy_cost: 0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    action_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    damage: 10,
    poise: 5,
    knockback: (direction: Away, strength: 3.0),
    radius: 4.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    dodgeable: Roll,
    destroy_terrain: None,
    eye_height: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Divine)),
)
